In commit https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36149/changes/12208a02ff5f795369fb2ab28884dc37b2db245d: _validation: keep pruned blocks in m_blocks_unlinked_

This still checks for pprev here:

https://github.com/enochaz/bitcoin/blob/532ffaa26d0557c149d7efee544f163fdcf84006/src/validation.cpp#L3840-L3843

But the else branch already guarantees pprev is non-null, and `AddUnlinkedBlock` now checks it as a precondition. I think it can be removed here. Leaving it is fine, but it feels redundant and might obscure the `BLOCK_VALID_TREE` condition for someone reading the code. 

